#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069592} :activity/id #uuid "a94cc1b0-429b-5583-ab2e-ced406c12a6a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048267 :topic/id #uuid "8dee6cdf-6bc7-52db-8873-a393c17a11e1" :topic/math-academy-id 384} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070024 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll learn how to solve equations that contain absolute value expressions.\n\nFor example, let's consider the following equation:\n\n$$\n|x+1| = 4\n$$\n\nFor this equation to be true, either the *positive or negative* of the expression inside the absolute value must equal the right-hand side. That is,\n\n$$\nx+1 = 4 \\qquad\\qquad \\text{ or } \\qquad\\qquad -(x+1)=4.\n$$\n\nSo, let's solve these two equations:\n\n- First, we solve the equation $x+1 = 4{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =4 \\\\ x+1-1 & =4-1 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve the equation $-(x+1) = 4{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+1) & =4 \\\\ -x-1 & =4 \\\\ -x-1+1 & =4+1 \\\\ -x & =5 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original absolute value equation are $x={\\color{blue}3}$ and $x={\\color{red}{-5}}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "35d16431-4611-59fc-8888-c1db1a7b9902" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8821 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "0212403d-0f66-5be5-8ebb-0dcacbe7f08f" :step/math-academy-id 143132 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069593}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070025 :tutorial/content "So, we've seen that the solutions to the equation \n\n$$\n|x+1| = 4\n$$\n\nare $x={\\color{blue}3}$ and $x={\\color{red}{-5}}.$ \n\nWe can verify that these solutions are correct by substituting them back into the original equation and checking we get a true statement:\n\n- Substituting $x={\\color{blue}3}$ into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+1| & =4 \\\\ |3+1| & =4 \\\\ |4| & =4 \\\\ 4 & =4.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x={\\color{blue}3}$ is indeed a solution to the absolute value equation.\n\n- Substituting $x={\\color{red}-5}$ into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+1| & =4 \\\\ |-5+1| & =4 \\\\ |-4| & =4 \\\\ 4 & =4.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x={\\color{red}-5}$ is indeed a solution to the absolute value equation.\n\nTherefore, $x={\\color{blue}3}$ and $x={\\color{red}{-5}}$ are both solutions to our absolute value equation." :tutorial/id #uuid "561ffe88-9340-5e0a-840a-6946f446a9f2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8822 :tutorial/title "Checking the Solution"} :step/id #uuid "88ed50f9-5a31-59c8-9fca-2e1513db0b7a" :step/math-academy-id 143133 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069594}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069594 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068709 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068489 :question/id #uuid "b5ef1eb1-4603-5d02-8478-94e8de89ad85" :question/math-academy-id "e-14216"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c402c36-0eaa-5281-a7b3-051a3f65e3f9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048725} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049844} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049939} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050613}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069080} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069117} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069118} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487290} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487370}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Absolute Value Equations"} :step/id #uuid "5413cce8-d1e6-5e3b-b122-54f31f20e10c" :step/math-academy-id 143134 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069595}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069595 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068710 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068490 :question/id #uuid "9dd0ea37-1775-577e-9e48-d82a50b28963" :question/math-academy-id "e-14221"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ee2e348-0af1-5e7d-a4b4-f3450ee9c19f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048673}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069119} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069120} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487299} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487349} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492915} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547009} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552472}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations"} :step/id #uuid "2e7e6f3f-5ced-591e-96c7-4cf8ac5ac6d1" :step/math-academy-id 143138 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069596}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069596 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068711 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068492 :question/id #uuid "9aa175ae-420f-5bef-855b-4f0aadbac062" :question/math-academy-id "e-14225"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61dbfea6-68e8-56b0-aae1-a48fdd8839b1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069073} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069121} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487288} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487325} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487387} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492899} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492905} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551343} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552475}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Absolute Value Equations With Negative Variable Coefficients"} :step/id #uuid "e9eff26c-6915-5c65-8459-e5a6a20e0ba1" :step/math-academy-id 143141 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069597}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069597 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068712 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068494 :question/id #uuid "094b2695-32c7-55dd-b3e1-27afcd3a09c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-14229"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ede7f82-5453-553b-b58e-31d7d9452336" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069074} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069127} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487335} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487369} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552406}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations Containing Fractions"} :step/id #uuid "6afe9233-9d29-545c-9bcc-718ed7ad41e6" :step/math-academy-id 143144}] :activity/title "Absolute Value Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068932}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046648} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492987} :activity/id #uuid "fdf293e8-c26a-525e-9d5d-8af56d0bc18f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048267 :topic/id #uuid "8dee6cdf-6bc7-52db-8873-a393c17a11e1" :topic/math-academy-id 384} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492975 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1745440e-88bf-5d51-8897-e4414167e24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-11$ or $-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492261} {:answer/id #uuid "614a5039-7de1-5dbf-bca4-d8ffc425678e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492413} {:answer/id #uuid "76d2fb58-4ccb-56f8-910a-14c6ece3d1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ or $11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492456} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ed8913-7141-5fed-a6ed-846233cc1d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$11$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492602} {:answer/id #uuid "f02f7135-1784-56eb-88e1-1c8c91546081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$1$ or $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492682}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492456} :answer-field/id #uuid "51aef6b7-5dcd-5253-a886-fdee125552e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b25ca648-9cf3-58f7-bad1-6cf2e59324cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-154645" :question/problem "If $|5-x|=6,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|5-x|=5-x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =6 \\\\ 5-x & =6 \\\\ -x & =1 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5-x|=-(5-x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =6 \\\\ -(5-x) & =6 \\\\ -5+x & =6 \\\\ x & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=11.$"} :step/id #uuid "a1c53633-2063-5148-ab3a-e83f6501d22e"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492987 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0701c6fb-b8b0-5030-bb54-6715655e1d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-\\frac{2}{7}$ or $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492232} {:answer/id #uuid "591e63f9-b0da-50e5-9f5f-c6dc29186793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-2$ or $-\\frac{2}{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492392} {:answer/id #uuid "8f3a1f6d-cc83-5713-9c86-11f797705b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{7}$ or $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492500} {:answer/id #uuid "a4bff5c8-756d-5c90-a938-61faf60d9476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-2$ or $\\frac{7}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492550} {:answer/id #uuid "b716a5c1-2bda-5fe2-a26b-d8a2524741b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ or $\\frac{7}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492586}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492586} :answer-field/id #uuid "dac4219c-b92c-5d85-9814-6729d48e7233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bf001cda-9f10-546a-97c2-0d9313d65e00" :question/math-academy-id "q-15254" :question/problem "If $|11-4x|=3,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|11-4x|=11-4x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|11-4x| & =3 \\\\ 11-4x & =3 \\\\ -4x & =-8 \\\\ \\frac{-4x}{-4} & =\\frac{-8}{-4} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|11-4x|=-(11-4x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|11-4x| & =3 \\\\ -(11-4x) & =3 \\\\ -11+4x & =3 \\\\ 4x & =14 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & =\\frac{14}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=2$ and $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "b16ab395-e781-5b4b-970d-5cc8a7610c9e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493001}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493001 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "589f4d35-5413-5d87-83c1-4a59ecc9ebd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{9}{5}$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492388} {:answer/id #uuid "9d463002-439b-562b-9798-0df675319b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492523} {:answer/id #uuid "b557add2-f5fc-5a0c-ad04-8a1c5f8ba3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-3$ or $\\frac{9}{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492580} {:answer/id #uuid "cc661ccb-9cb1-5767-b7fa-3f7b29153ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$1$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492623} {:answer/id #uuid "e68b697d-110c-5bd9-88a6-6ccd86dd44e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-3$ or $-\\frac{9}{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492664}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492388} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffecce80-4a83-596b-bd4c-c3a2d3d4cfc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc058aee-cd4e-56a4-b735-dc759e998e0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-15257" :question/problem "If $|5x-12|=3,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|5x-12|=5x-12,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-12| & =3 \\\\ 5x-12 & =3 \\\\ 5x & =15 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5x-12|=-(5x-12),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-12| & =3 \\\\ -(5x-12) & =3 \\\\ -5x+12 & =3 \\\\ -5x & =-9 \\\\ \\frac{-5x}{-5} & =\\frac{-9}{-5} \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{9}{5}$ and $x=3.$"} :step/id #uuid "e83a3e23-66a2-56f7-b2eb-d3f3cc24ff4f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492975}}] :activity/title "Absolute Value Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492222}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552584} :activity/id #uuid "e0b82c9f-d695-577c-9c14-8e632f759242" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048267 :topic/id #uuid "8dee6cdf-6bc7-52db-8873-a393c17a11e1" :topic/math-academy-id 384} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552545 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad87764-6044-5767-902d-f845c340fce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-3$ or $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551881} {:answer/id #uuid "7236c074-3016-5112-a3b9-0ad8989ea929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-12$ or $-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551936} {:answer/id #uuid "9133a202-35d2-56e1-8e7d-2d811e679fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-18$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552019} {:answer/id #uuid "b0458107-3a29-5b00-817a-03a49afcbbfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$12$ or $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552090} {:answer/id #uuid "e42a61a8-e821-58ec-be90-1c90c3e1e586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$6$ or $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552193}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551881} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7cd6986-58f2-5df8-9623-61bd4f8f7c74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0fd09d79-cd92-571a-b908-4f0df92196ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-154703" :question/problem "If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=5,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=3-\\frac{2}{3}y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-\\frac{2}{3}y| & =5 \\\\ 3-\\frac{2}{3}y & =5 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $-\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3}y & =2 \\\\ (-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}y) & =(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (2) \\\\ (\\cancel{-\\frac{3}{2}})\\cdot (\\cancel{-\\frac{2}{3}}y) & =-\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ y & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=-(3-\\frac{2}{3}y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-\\frac{2}{3}y| & =5 \\\\ -(3-\\frac{2}{3}y) & =5 \\\\ -3+\\frac{2}{3}y & =5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y & =8 \\\\ (\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}y) & =(\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (8) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{3}{2}})\\cdot (\\cancel{\\frac{2}{3}}y) & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\ y & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-3$ and $y=12.$"} :step/id #uuid "2681db7c-ff74-52ae-b2fb-ee80f155348c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552587}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552584 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057a12b0-d4bc-55a8-9eee-258d1a00e98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-\\frac{2}{3}$ or $\\frac{13}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551674} {:answer/id #uuid "23f8c6a8-ae4e-54ef-88f9-fe179de5f44d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ or $\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551745} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ed2067-bb69-58be-ba14-334cd4747618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ or $\\frac{13}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552189} {:answer/id #uuid "efc542f6-65a8-5ed6-9840-e880355816ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{2}$ or $\\frac{11}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552226} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9c7d02-30df-5e21-a713-ce0444cf2812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{2}$ or $\\frac{13}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552251} :answer-field/id #uuid "4000b40a-b454-50f7-9046-7cb530cbcdff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ff91a7b-d943-550d-955e-e036467fba09" :question/math-academy-id "q-112200" :question/problem "If $|8-2x|=5,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|8-2x|=8-2x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|8-2x| & =5 \\\\ 8-2x & =5 \\\\ -2x & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2} & =\\frac{-3}{-2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|8-2x|=-(8-2x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|8-2x| & =5 \\\\ -(8-2x) & =5 \\\\ -8+2x & =5 \\\\ 2x & =13 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{13}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{13}{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "95f6f89f-3826-5c24-91ad-1310088d28de" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552545}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552587 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a250bff-7cf2-5b8c-a70c-561cb671e351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551762}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551762} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ccce716-e2da-5a85-b47b-a94871a52a3a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86409c3b-54a1-5d16-aabc-60ec0b435025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551987}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551987} :answer-field/id #uuid "6808506c-1a45-5a20-8d53-0017152fbabe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8bfe078d-4df3-523f-8453-0c2505e6812e" :question/math-academy-id "q-215127" :question/problem "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|5y-1|=6$ are $y=${{field-1}} and $y=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|5y-1|=5y-1,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5y-1| & =6 \\\\ 5y-1 & =6 \\\\ 5y & =7 \\\\ \\frac{5y}{5} & =\\frac{7}{5} \\\\ y & =\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5y-1|=-(5y-1),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5y-1| & =6 \\\\ -(5y-1) & =6 \\\\ -5y+1 & =6 \\\\ -5y & =5 \\\\ \\frac{-5y}{-5} & =\\frac{5}{-5} \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $y=-1$ and $y=\\frac{7}{5}.$"} :step/id #uuid "99735047-5749-5b1b-8081-cfbe6b269602"}] :activity/title "Absolute Value Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551662}]}
